 6. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 The Devil Ray T24 unmanned surface vessel. Photo: Courtesy of MARTAC

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 🌊 The Taiwan Coast Guard Administration is acquiring an undisclosed number of Devil Ray T24s made by American company MARTAC. The deal includes a co-production agreement with Taiwan's Confucian Co.

 Why it matters: "This pursuit by the Taiwan Coast Guard represents a landmark moment for MARTAC and for the adoption of unmanned surface vessels in the Indo-Pacific region," Seamus Flatley, MARTAC's chief growth officer, said in a statement. 💭 My thought bubble: It only makes sense for Taipei to stockpile drone boats. 📡 Austin Sensing Company emerged from stealth with $15 million in funding, including an $11 million seed. Backers include Bling Capital, Draper Associates and Ensemble VC.

 Why it matters: CEO Tucker Dordevic was named the Premier Lacrosse League's rookie of the year in 2023 and has a background in aerospace-and-defense banking. "I loved working with people building physical things," he told me, "in a space that was really cool." 💭 My thought bubble: Tectonic broke the news . (And Dordevic was a very fun interview.) 🪽 Aevex is "prepping for" an air-launched variant of its Specter deep-strike drone, chief technology officer Manan Patel told me on the sidelines of the Association of the U.S. Army conference .

 Why it matters: "Once we design this airframe architecture, we're able to make it bigger and smaller based on what the mission needs are," he said. "You go from requirements to production in months, versus years." 💭 My thought bubble: Deep-strike drones are becoming a market unto themselves. Thank Ukraine for the inspiration. 
 
